{"id":"mahabharata-12-298","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":298,"title":"अष्टनवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 298 · Yajnavalkya and Janaka: what is beyond dharma","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks about that which is free of dharma and adharma, birth and death, merit and sin, and Bhishma tells how Yajnavalkya taught Janaka. Yajnavalkya says that from egoism came the mind and the qualities of the elements, which is the third creation.","kn":"ಧರ್ಮ-ಅಧರ್ಮ, ಜನ್ಮ-ಮೃತ್ಯು, ಪುಣ್ಯ-ಪಾಪದಿಂದ ಮುಕ್ತವಾದುದರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯಾಜ್ಞವಲ್ಕ್ಯ ಜನಕನಿಗೆ ಬೋಧಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಹಂಕಾರದಿಂದ ಮನಸ್ಸು ಮತ್ತು ಭೂತಗುಣಗಳು ಹುಟ್ಟಿದವು, ಇದು ಮೂರನೆಯ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर धर्म-अधर्म, जन्म-मृत्यु और पुण्य-पाप से मुक्त तत्त्व के बारे में पूछते हैं, और भीष्म याज्ञवल्क्य द्वारा जनक को दिया उपदेश सुनाते हैं। याज्ञवल्क्य कहते हैं कि अहंकार से मन और भूतगुण उपजे, यह तीसरी सृष्टि है।","te":"ధర్మాధర్మాలు, జన్మమృత్యువులు, పుణ్యపాపాల నుండి విముక్తమైనది గురించి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; యాజ్ఞవల్క్యుడు జనకునికి బోధించిన తీరును భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. అహంకారం నుండి మనసు, భూత గుణాలు పుట్టాయని, ఇది మూడవ సృష్టి అని యాజ్ఞవల్క్యుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"அறம் அறமின்மை, பிறப்பு இறப்பு, புண்ணியம் பாவத்திலிருந்து விடுபட்டதைப் பற்றி யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, யாஜ்ஞவல்க்யர் ஜனகனுக்குப் போதித்ததைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். அகங்காரத்திலிருந்து மனமும் பூத குணங்களும் தோன்றின, இது மூன்றாம் படைப்பு என்கிறார் யாஜ்ஞவல்க்யர்.","ml":"ധർമ്മത്തിനും അധർമ്മത്തിനും, ജനനത്തിനും മരണത്തിനും, പുണ്യത്തിനും പാപത്തിനും അതീതമായതെന്തെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; യാജ്ഞവൽക്യൻ ജനകന് ഉപദേശിച്ചതെന്തെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. അഹംഭാവത്തിൽനിന്ന് മനസ്സും മൂലകങ്ങളുടെ ഗുണങ്ങളും ഉണ്ടായി എന്നും, അത് മൂന്നാമത്തെ സൃഷ്ടിയാണെന്നും യാജ്ഞവൽക്യൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.298; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धर्माधर्मविमुक्तं यद्विमुक्तं सर्वसंश्रयात् ।\nजन्ममृत्युविमुक्तं च विमुक्तं पुण्यपापयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That which is free of dharma and adharma, free of all dependence, free of birth and death, free of merit and sin..."}},{"n":2,"text":"यच्छिवं नित्यमभयं नित्यं चाक्षरमव्ययम् ।\nशुचि नित्यमनायासं तद्भवान्वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"...which is auspicious, eternal, fearless, imperishable and unchanging, pure, effortless: please tell me of that."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्र ते वर्तयिष्येऽहमितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nयाज्ञवल्क्यस्य संवादं जनकस्य च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this I shall tell you an ancient account, Bharata: the conversation of Yajnavalkya and Janaka."}},{"n":4,"text":"याज्ञवल्क्यमृषिश्रेष्ठं दैवरातिर्महायशाः ।\nपप्रच्छ जनको राजा प्रश्नं प्रश्नविदां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Janaka, son of Devarata, of great fame and the best of those who know how to question, asked the question of Yajnavalkya, best of sages."}},{"n":5,"text":"कतीन्द्रियाणि विप्रर्षे कति प्रकृतयः स्मृताः ।\nकिमव्यक्तं परं ब्रह्म तस्माच्च परतस्तु किम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How many senses are there, brahmin sage, and how many natures are taught? What is the unmanifest, the supreme Brahman, and what lies beyond it?\""}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रभवं चाप्ययं चैव कालसंख्यां तथैव च ।\nवक्तुमर्हसि विप्रेन्द्र त्वदनुग्रहकाङ्क्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Chief of brahmins, please tell me also of origin and dissolution and the reckoning of time, for I seek your grace.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अज्ञानात्परिपृच्छामि त्वं हि ज्ञानमयो निधिः ।\nतदहं श्रोतुमिच्छामि सर्वमेतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask from ignorance, for you are a treasure made of knowledge; I wish to hear all this without doubt.\""}},{"text":"याज्ञवल्क्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yajnavalkya said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"श्रूयतामवनीपाल यदेतदनुपृच्छसि ।\nयोगानां परमं ज्ञानं सांख्यानां च विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, protector of the earth, to what you ask, the supreme knowledge of Yogis and especially of the Sankhyas."}},{"n":9,"text":"न तवाविदितं किंचिन्मां तु जिज्ञासते भवान् ।\nपृष्टेन चापि वक्तव्यमेष धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing is unknown to you; you are testing me. And what is asked must be answered; this is the eternal dharma."}},{"n":10,"text":"अष्टौ प्रकृतयः प्रोक्ता विकाराश्चापि षोडश ।\nअथ सप्त तु व्यक्तानि प्राहुरध्यात्मचिन्तकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eight natures are taught, and sixteen modifications; and those who reflect on the Self speak of seven manifest things besides."}},{"n":11,"text":"अव्यक्तं च महांश्चैव तथाहंकार एव च ।\nपृथिवी वायुराकाशमापो ज्योतिश्च पञ्चमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are the unmanifest, the great principle, egoism, earth, air, space, water, and fire as the fifth."}},{"n":12,"text":"एताः प्रकृतयस्त्वष्टौ विकारानपि मे शृणु ।\nश्रोत्रं त्वक्चैव चक्षुश्च जिह्वा घ्राणं च पञ्चमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the eight natures; now hear the modifications from me: hearing, skin, eye, tongue, and nose as the fifth..."}},{"n":13,"text":"शब्दस्पर्शौ च रूपं च रसो गन्धस्तथैव च ।\nवाक्च हस्तौ च पादौ च पायुर्मेढ्रं तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"...sound, touch, form, taste and smell, speech, the two hands, the two feet, the organ of excretion and the organ of generation."}},{"n":14,"text":"एते विशेषा राजेन्द्र महाभूतेषु पञ्चसु ।\nबुद्धीन्द्रियाण्यथैतानि सविशेषाणि मैथिल ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the specifics, king, in the five great elements; and these are the senses of knowledge together with their specifics, king of Mithila."}},{"n":15,"text":"मनः षोडशकं प्राहुरध्यात्मगतिचिन्तकाः ।\nत्वं चैवान्ये च विद्वांसस्तत्त्वबुद्धिविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who reflect on the course of the Self say the mind is the sixteenth; you and other learned ones are skilled in the intellect of principles."}},{"n":16,"text":"अव्यक्ताच्च महानात्मा समुत्पद्यति पार्थिव ।\nप्रथमं सर्गमित्येतदाहुः प्राधानिकं बुधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the unmanifest the great Self arises, king; the wise call this the first creation, the one of primal Nature."}},{"n":17,"text":"महतश्चाप्यहंकार उत्पद्यति नराधिप ।\nद्वितीयं सर्गमित्याहुरेतद्बुद्ध्यात्मकं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the great principle egoism arises, lord of men; they call it the second creation, held to be of the nature of intellect."}},{"n":18,"text":"अहंकाराच्च संभूतं मनो भूतगुणात्मकम् ।\nतृतीयः सर्ग इत्येष आहंकारिक उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"From egoism arises the mind, of the nature of the qualities of the elements; this is the third creation, called that of egoism."}},{"n":19,"text":"मनसस्तु समुद्भूता महाभूता नराधिप ।\nचतुर्थं सर्गमित्येतन्मानसं परिचक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the mind the great elements arise, lord of men; they call this the fourth creation, the mental one."}},{"n":20,"text":"शब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च रसो गन्धस्तथैव च ।\nपञ्चमं सर्गमित्याहुर्भौतिकं भूतचिन्तकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sound, touch, form, taste and smell: those who study the elements call this the fifth creation, the elemental."}},{"n":21,"text":"श्रोत्रं त्वक्चैव चक्षुश्च जिह्वा घ्राणं च पञ्चमम् ।\nसर्गं तु षष्ठमित्याहुर्बहुचिन्तात्मकं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing, skin, eye, tongue and nose as the fifth: they call this the sixth creation, held to be full of many thoughts."}},{"n":22,"text":"अधः श्रोत्रेन्द्रियग्राम उत्पद्यति नराधिप ।\nसप्तमं सर्गमित्याहुरेतदैन्द्रियकं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The group of hearing and the other senses arises below, lord of men; they call this the seventh creation, held to be of the senses."}},{"n":23,"text":"ऊर्ध्वस्रोतस्तथा तिर्यगुत्पद्यति नराधिप ।\nअष्टमं सर्गमित्याहुरेतदार्जवकं बुधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What flows upward and sideways arises, lord of men; the wise call this the eighth creation, the straight one."}},{"n":24,"text":"तिर्यक्स्रोतस्त्वधःस्रोत उत्पद्यति नराधिप ।\nनवमं सर्गमित्याहुरेतदार्जवकं बुधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What flows sideways and downward arises, lord of men; the wise call this the ninth creation, the straight one."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतानि नव सर्गाणि तत्त्वानि च नराधिप ।\nचतुर्विंशतिरुक्तानि यथाश्रुति निदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These nine creations and the principles, lord of men, are told as twenty-four, according to the tradition's illustration."}},{"n":26,"text":"अत ऊर्ध्वं महाराज गुणस्यैतस्य तत्त्वतः ।\nमहात्मभिरनुप्रोक्तां कालसंख्यां निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beyond this, great king, hear from me the reckoning of time for this quality, as stated by the great-souled."}}]}]}